 "notes": "CASTLEBEEF #112. Glowing lines are the paths. Start in the barrel (front top right), exit on the back (stone ring, centre). Front has no spin; back spins at (0.20,0.07) and (0.43,0.48). Doubts: the back image looks horizontally mirrored (EXIT and CASTLE BEEF text read reversed), and the side flip triangles do not line up in y with the front (front left 0.36/0.74, right 0.33/0.75; back left 0.26/0.67, right 0.25/0.63), so flip-pair warnings are expected; pairing intended is probably upper with upper and lower with lower. Front top: two branches from the top flip each through a door (0.46,0.27 right / 0.57,0.27 up) to the castle cross; assumed both reach the y 0.37 horizontal. Route not fully verified: with no front spin, rotation is only possible on the back; reaching exit door (0.48,0.31, arrow down) needs the card upside down, presumably via the back top-left spin loop or lower loop spin.",
